# Film Chemistry & Camera Optics Taste & Aesthetics Cache
#
# Aesthetic philosophy, organic silver grain vs Cartesian pixels, vintage optical flaws, and archival permanence.

#>spw_cache_film_optics_taste
#:cache #!film_optics_taste
#:layer #!pragmatics

^"intent"{
  ~#goal: "Articulate the aesthetic philosophy, wonder considerations, and tactile taste of photochemical film stocks, organic crystal grain structure, and cinematographic lens character."
  ~#protocol: "cache.layer/1"
}

^"taste_principles"{
  "grain_as_living_substance": .{
    organic_randomness: "Silver halide crystals distribute across three-dimensional gelatin depths with stochastic Poisson randomness; no two frames share identical grain lattices, imparting an organic temporal shimmer that digital sensor noise cannot replicate",
    highlight_shoulder_grace: "Film negative rolls off extreme highlights through an asymptotic logarithmic shoulder, preserving delicate micro-contrast in fire, sun reflections, and white silk where digital sensors clip abruptly to 8-bit or 10-bit numerical maximums",
    temporal_dither: "At 24 frames per second, the shifting crystal grain pattern acts as a continuous spatio-temporal dither filter, resolving fine perceived detail beyond the static resolving power of a single frozen frame",
  }[reg=facet],
  "optical_imperfection_as_emotional_voice": .{
    rejection_of_clinical_sterility: "Modern computer-aided ray-traced lenses with complex aspheric surfaces achieve near-perfect MTF curves but can strip cinema of mystery, rendering faces clinical and unforgiving",
    character_of_vintage_glass: "Single coatings, subtle field curvature, controlled spherical aberration, and non-telecentric exits create an organic depth separation—a sense of air and roundness around the actor",
    anamorphic_lyricism: "The stretched oval out-of-focus background disc and horizontal blue flare are not technical flaws to be eradicated, but expressive optical metaphors for memory, grandeur, and romantic drama",
  }[reg=facet],
  "tactile_permanence_and_archival_longevity": .{
    physical_silver_record: "Black-and-white silver gelatin negative on ESTAR polyester base stored at 2 degrees C and 20% relative humidity has an estimated lifespan exceeding 500 years, needing only white light and an optical lens to decode",
    digital_fragility: "Digital files exist hostage to magnetic media decay, proprietary codec obsolescence, cloud subscription models, and bit-rot; photochemical film remains human civilization's most resilient visual archive",
  }[reg=facet],
}

^"wonder_probes"{
  #>wonder_film_optics_taste_1
  ?["Why does motion picture film grain evoke an unconscious emotional sensation of nostalgia and tactile memory, even in generations who grew up exclusively with high-definition digital screens?"]{
    #:depth #!philosophical ~#lens(photochemical_perceptual_phenomenology)
    ~#hypothesis: "Film grain mirrors biological vision: human retinal rod and cone photoreceptors are non-uniform, stochastically distributed biological sensors that continually refresh with micro-saccades. A film frame's stochastic silver grain aligns with our physiological visual perception, whereas rigid Cartesian pixel grids impose an artificial mathematical rigidity that the unconscious mind detects as synthetic."
    !probe{ "Conduct eye-tracking and neural pupillometry studies comparing subject engagement during projection of 35mm film print vs 4K digital uncompressed scan of identical scenes." }
    $%[psychology.visual_cortex_dither_response, aesthetics.stochastic_retinal_resonance]
  }

  #>wonder_film_optics_taste_2
  ?["How does the physical resistance of working with a 400-foot magazine (yielding only 4 minutes and 26 seconds of 35mm film) alter the psychology and artistic presence of director and actor on set?"]{
    #:depth #!craft ~#lens(scarcity_induced_mindfulness)
    ~#hypothesis: "The auditory clatter of the mechanical camera movement and the tangible economic cost of running emulsion induce acute situational mindfulness. Rehearsals intensify, actors commit with raw vulnerability on take one or two, and crew silence becomes sacred, transforming filmmaking from infinite digital iteration into an existential, high-stakes theatrical ritual."
    !probe{ "Analyze take count, director note frequency, and heart-rate variability across cast and crew on productions alternating between 35mm film packages and unlimited digital camera packages." }
    $%[sociology.set_discipline_metrics, psychology.scarcity_presence_index]
  }
}
